+# Comment Escape browser check
+
+Requires Cargo, Chrome and `playwright-cli`. From the checkout, build and start a
+fresh throwaway daemon:
+
+```sh
+cargo build --locked --target-dir /tmp/jelly-escape-target
+/tmp/jelly-escape-target/debug/jelly serve --port 17883 --home /tmp/jelly-escape-home
+# In another terminal, from the checkout:
+/tmp/jelly-escape-target/debug/jelly --url http://127.0.0.1:17883 new escape:map \
+  --view skill/recipes/map/view.html --verbs skill/recipes/map/verbs.js \
+  --state skill/recipes/map/state.json
+```
+
+From a scratch directory, run with an absolute path to the script:
+
+```sh
+playwright-cli -s=escape open http://127.0.0.1:17883/
+playwright-cli -s=escape run-code --filename=/path/to/jelly/tests/comment-escape.js
+playwright-cli -s=escape close
+```
+
+The check uses the real runtime and map recipe, standalone and in the full-view
+iframe. It advances to step 3, checks that Escape cancels commenting and the
+comment editor without losing the step, then checks ordinary Escape still
+dismisses the trace. It fails on the pre-fix runtime. Stop the throwaway daemon
+after testing; no real jelly home is used.
+
